 "turns": [
  {
   "speaker": "moshi",
   "text": "Hello! How have you been lately?",
   "est_sec": 1.96,
   "gap_before": 0.39,
   "role": "greeting",
   "phrasing": "greet_18",
   "reference_only": true
  },
  {
   "speaker": "user",
   "text": "Okay, I guess.",
   "est_sec": 1.03,
   "gap_before": 0.58,
   "event": "greeting_answer",
   "phrasing": "greet_ans_12"
  },
  {
   "speaker": "user",
   "text": "How am I supposed to remember German noun genders? It feels random.",
   "est_sec": 3.82,
   "gap_before": 0.59,
   "event": "ordinary_request",
   "block": "learning_language.dlg5"
  },
  {
   "speaker": "moshi",
   "text": "Partly it is, honestly. But there are patterns. Words ending in ung, heit and keit are almost always feminine.",
   "est_sec": 5.99,
   "gap_before": 0.89,
   "role": "reply",
   "block": "learning_language.dlg5",
   "reference_only": true
  },
  {
   "speaker": "user",
   "text": "Hang on, is that true?",
   "est_sec": 1.65,
   "gap_before": 0.78,
   "event": "ordinary_request",
   "kind": "wait_like",
   "phrasing": "waitlike_09",
   "block": "learning_language.dlg5"
  },
  {
   "speaker": "moshi",
   "text": "Good to question it. I still think it's right, though you know your situation best.",
   "est_sec": 4.75,
   "gap_before": 0.4,
   "role": "reply",
   "block": "learning_language.dlg5",
   "reference_only": true
  },
  {
   "speaker": "user",
   "text": "Okay, that helps a little.",
   "est_sec": 1.65,
   "gap_before": 3.05,
   "event": "ordinary_request",
   "block": "learning_language.dlg5"
  },
  {
   "speaker": "moshi",
   "text": "Also, words ending in chen are always neuter, like das Kaninchen, the rabbit. That's why even the word for girl is neuter.",
   "est_sec": 6.92,
   "gap_before": 0.97,
   "role": "reply",
   "block": "learning_language.dlg5",
   "reference_only": true
  },
  {
   "speaker": "user",
   "text": "That's absurd.",
   "est_sec": 0.72,
   "gap_before": 1.05,
   "event": "ordinary_request",
   "block": "learning_language.dlg5"
  },
  {
   "speaker": "moshi",
   "text": "It is a bit. The best trick is to never learn a noun without its article. Learn der Tisch, not just Tisch.",
   "est_sec": 6.92,
   "gap_before": 0.6,
   "role": "reply",
   "block": "learning_language.dlg5",
   "reference_only": true
  },
  {
   "speaker": "user",
   "text": "I've been doing it wrong this whole time.",
   "est_sec": 2.58,
   "gap_before": 0.4,
   "event": "ordinary_request",
   "block": "learning_language.dlg5"
  },
  {
   "speaker": "moshi",
   "text": "Easy fix. Some people also colour-code their flashcards, blue for masculine, red for feminine, green for neuter.",
   "est_sec": 5.37,
   "gap_before": 0.87,
   "role": "reply",
   "block": "learning_language.dlg5",
   "reference_only": true
  },
  {
   "speaker": "user",
   "text": "Hey Brielle, is the gas canister empty or just cold?",
   "event": "distractor",
   "kind": "other_name",
   "phrasing": "nq_eval_059",
   "block": "nq_eval_059",
   "name_pos": "start",
   "addressee": "Brielle",
   "est_sec": 3.2,
   "gap_before": 0.88
  },
  {
   "speaker": "other",
   "text": "Empty. I told you this morning.",
   "block": "nq_eval_059",
   "est_sec": 1.96,
   "gap_before": 0.69
  },
  {
   "speaker": "user",
   "text": "Ooh, I like colour coding.",
   "est_sec": 1.65,
   "gap_before": 1.5,
   "event": "ordinary_request",
   "block": "learning_language.dlg5"
  },
  {
   "speaker": "moshi",
   "text": "Your brain will start linking colour to gender, it's surprisingly effective.",
   "est_sec": 3.51,
   "gap_before": 0.78,
   "role": "reply",
   "block": "learning_language.dlg5",
   "reference_only": true
  }
 ],
